<% content_for :title, "About — ThoughtVault" %>

<div class="row">
  <div class="col-md-8">
    <h2>&#128218; About ThoughtVault</h2>
    <p class="lead text-muted">Preserving wisdom from the world's greatest thinkers.</p>
    <hr>

    <h5>What is ThoughtVault?</h5>
    <p>
      ThoughtVault is a community platform where collectors can save, organise and share their
      favourite quotes from philosophers, scientists, writers and other great minds throughout
      history. Whether you're drawn to ancient Stoicism or modern political thought, ThoughtVault
      gives you a personal library for the ideas that matter to you.
    </p>

    <h5>How it works</h5>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Create a free account</strong> to start your own quote collection.</li>
      <li><strong>Add quotes</strong>, tag them by philosophical category, and link them to their thinker.</li>
      <li><strong>Mark quotes as public</strong> to share them with the community, or keep them private.</li>
      <li><strong>Browse and search</strong> the public collection by category or author name — no account required.</li>
    </ul>

    <h5>Quote Categories</h5>
    <p>
      ThoughtVault supports the following philosophical categories:
      Metaphysics, Axiology, Epistemology, Logic, Ethics, Political Philosophy, and Aesthetics.
    </p>

    <h5>Built with</h5>
    <p>Ruby on Rails &bull; SQLite 3 &bull; Bootstrap 5</p>
  </div>
</div>
